package api

import (
	"net/http"
)

var _ = declareRoute(routeDecl{
	Method:      http.MethodGet,
	Pattern:     "/api/v1/projects/{key}/evals/{slug}/items",
	Auth:        authAny,
	Description: "The rows behind an eval's numbers over the window and the compare range, one page {items, total, limit, offset, min_n}, every row {row_key, row_kind, cols, measured_at, source, href, links, range} whatever its kind, range compare for a row of the compare range: the eval's readings (a reading logged under a computed eval's slug among them), its stored day rows (day), and for a computed eval the rows its numbers count, as its project's day rows counted them: a Legion eval's issues closed in the range and legion-splitting's filings (issue), a delivery eval's pull requests and deploy runs (pull_request, deploy), a CI eval's runs (run) and pr-ci's jobs (job), unowned-p0's open P0 issues with no owner (issue), code-survival-30d's changes (change, keyed <repo>@<sha>: cols sha, pr_number, group, issue, added, alive, share and via_repository; href its pull request, a via link to its commit; under survival:<g> of its group) and post-merge-rework-30d's pairs (pair, a change and a later change that removed its lines by its 30-day mark, keyed <repo>@<adder>><remover>: cols adder_issue, remover_issue, kind, lines, days_between, adder_pr, remover_pr and group; href the remover's pull request, a via link to the remover's commit and a related link to the adder's; under the series of its kind and its adder's group, rework:<g>, iteration:<g>, noissue:<g> or other:<g>, a pair where either change has no issue under noissue:<g> alone with that issue null; other:<g> also counts the lines that commits which merged no pull request removed, which no pair row stands for), each where the status row of its day says the day was measured. Both code evals also answer each reason the range reads no data other than days still waiting (absent, under every series, cols.cause): marked (a day a force-push marked: day, repo and sha, the day's first change, which is its href, or the project's settings page where it holds none), blocked (a commit whose patch GitHub gave neither whole nor on files[]: sha, files (the files GitHub listed on files[] with no patch), unlisted (true where the files[] listing may not hold the whole commit: it listed GitHub's limit of 3,000 files, named no stats, or its entries change fewer lines than the commit's stats count), reason, repo and the days of the range it blocks; its href and a via link are the commit), repo_unreadable (the default repository the App cannot read, with the reason), no_default_repo (where the project has no default repository and holds no day row of the eval, whatever the range) and no_group, the last three addressed to the project's settings page, /projects/{key}/settings, with no link. measured_at is when a row's value was measured, the moment its eval dates it by: a reading's own, a pull request's merge, a deploy run's and a CI run's start, a Legion issue's close, a filing's filing, a day row's day, a job's newest day, a failing job's latest failure, a change's commit and a pair's adder's, a marked day its day and a blocking commit the oldest day of the range it blocks, and the read itself for an open P0 issue with no owner and for an absent row of a setting. ?series= narrows to a series (a Legion series' :roots or :children cut, a filed:<class> series, a job:<name> series, a code eval's group series), ?row_kind= and ?row= to a row kind and a row key, ?repo=, repeated, to those repositories (at most 100, a repeated one counted once, each name of at most 512 bytes); ?sort=median answers pr-ci's jobs with their series' min_n timed results, slowest first, and names the floor it ranked by in min_n (that min_n, and 1 where it is none, since a job needs a timed result to have a median), and ?sort=failures the jobs that failed in the 24 hours before the range's end; min_n is null for every other read. 400 INVALID_QUERY names a malformed key, a repo list or name past its bound, or a key the route does not take (any but these and the global session parameter), 404 PROJECT_NOT_FOUND and EVAL_NOT_FOUND as the eval's read answers them.",
	Handler:     (*server).listProjectEvalItems,
	Read:        readEntry{Writes: readWritesNothing},
	Shape: routeShape{
		Status: http.StatusOK, Response: evalItemsResponse{}, Params: evalItemsQuery{},
	},
})
